{
  "info": {
    "name": "DesApp — Autenticación y Catálogo",
    "description": "Alta, login, ApiKey y catálogo de jugadores de prueba. Casos positivos y negativos completos para testear el back a mano o con el Collection Runner / newman. Correr en orden (folder por folder, request por request): varias requests dependen de variables que setean las anteriores (userEmail, accessToken, apiKey, previousApiKey, playerId). Ver specs/001-user-auth/, specs/002-api-key-issuance/ y specs/004-player-catalog/.",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json"
  },
  "variable": [
    { "key": "baseUrl", "value": "http://localhost:3000" },
    { "key": "userEmail", "value": "" },
    { "key": "accessToken", "value": "" },
    { "key": "apiKey", "value": "" },
    { "key": "previousApiKey", "value": "" },
    { "key": "playerId", "value": "" }
  ],
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "Feature 1 — Auth (register, login, me)",
      "description": "Casos no reproducibles a mano en esta colección (sólo cubiertos por los e2e automatizados en backend/test/): JWT vencido (requiere firmar con el JWT_SECRET real del servidor, que no vive acá) y JWT válido de un usuario borrado (requiere manipular la base entre requests).",
      "item": [
        {
          "name": "Register — alta válida (201)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('201 Created', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(201); });",
                  "pm.test('no devuelve token ni contraseña', function () {",
                  "  const body = pm.response.json();",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('accessToken');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('password');",
                  "  pm.expect(body).to.not.have.property('passwordHash');",
                  "});",
                  "if (pm.response.code === 201) {",
                  "  pm.collectionVariables.set('userEmail', pm.response.json().email);",
                  "}"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "register"] },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{$randomEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"Abcd1234!\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "201 Created con { id, email, createdAt }. El test-script guarda el email real (devuelto por el server) en userEmail para las siguientes requests."
          }
        },
        {
          "name": "Register — email ya existe (409)",
          "event": [
            {
              "listen": "test",
              "script": {
                "type": "text/javascript",
                "exec": [
                  "pm.test('409 Conflict', function () { pm.response.to.have.status(409); });",
                  "pm.test('mensaje en español', function () {",
                  "  pm.expect(pm.response.json().message).to.eql('El email ya está registrado.');",
                  "});"
                ]
              }
            }
          ],
          "request": {
            "method": "POST",
            "header": [{ "key": "Content-Type", "value": "application/json" }],
            "url": { "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/auth/register", "host": ["{{baseUrl}}"], "path": ["auth", "register"] },
            "body": {
              "mode": "raw",
              "raw": "{\n  \"email\": \"{{userEmail}}\",\n  \"password\": \"Abcd1234!\"\n}"
            },
            "description": "Requiere haber corrido antes 'Register — alta válida' (usa userEmail). 409 porque el email ya está registrado."
          }
        },
        {
